1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,333
<i> Joey!</i>

2
00:00:01,467 --> 00:00:02,300
<i> Miguel?</i>

3
00:00:02,433 --> 00:00:03,433
<i> You're alive...</i>

4
00:00:03,567 --> 00:00:05,800
<i>Does this mean you'll reveal
yourself?</i>

5
00:00:05,933 --> 00:00:07,000
<i> We'll be together again?</i>

6
00:00:07,133 --> 00:00:09,333
<i>No, my child.
I need to finish my mission.</i>

7
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:11,700
<i> I only came here to see you.</i>

8
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:15,400
<i> Andrew was telling me
about his coverage in the north.</i>

9
00:00:15,533 --> 00:00:16,400
<i> Drug deal.</i>

10
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:19,267
<i>Unfortunately,
the mastermind escaped.</i>

11
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,633
<i> Was the deal finalized?</i>

12
00:00:20,767 --> 00:00:22,700
<i> Unfortunately, not.</i>

13
00:00:22,833 --> 00:00:25,133
<i> - Tomas, is that blood?
- I'll just change this bandage.</i>

14
00:00:25,267 --> 00:00:26,600
<i> But it's just his back.</i>

15
00:00:26,733 --> 00:00:28,300
<i>How can we build a case
with that?</i>

16
00:00:28,433 --> 00:00:29,467
<i> No face, no profile.</i>

17
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,767
<i>I picked this up
when Berdugo was escaping.</i>

18
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,800
<i>- There's something engraved.
- Maybe those are initials.</i>

19
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:37,100
<i>What's more important?
Andrew or your business?</i>

20
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:40,800
<i>Nothing is more important
to me than my family.</i>

21
00:00:40,933 --> 00:00:44,233
<i>Find a way to get rid of him.
No trace, no noise.</i>

22
00:00:44,367 --> 00:00:45,800
<i> My pleasure, Boss.</i>

23
00:01:05,367 --> 00:01:10,867
I'm aware Joey can't join
the raid.

24
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:14,500
But in my understanding,
she can...

25
00:01:14,633 --> 00:01:16,300
She can still be part of it,
I mean.

26
00:01:16,433 --> 00:01:19,000
Even in pre-planning.

27
00:01:19,133 --> 00:01:22,133
But you invoked protocol.

28
00:01:22,267 --> 00:01:25,167
That's why she was cut out
completely, right?

29
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,967
And it feels like...

30
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:30,733
I betrayed her.

31
00:01:30,867 --> 00:01:34,467
So, I just want to know
if it's really just protocol

32
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,433
or was it meant to...

33
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:38,733
cut her out completely.

34
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:44,067
Andrew, if I wanted to shut her
out because she was an obstacle,

35
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:47,133
I would never use my position.

36
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:51,333
I wouldn't hide behind protocol.

37
00:01:51,467 --> 00:01:53,700
Andrew, we have history,

38
00:01:55,033 --> 00:01:56,400
memories.

39
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:59,233
We have a past that you
and she don't have,

40
00:01:59,367 --> 00:02:01,333
and that can't be erased.

41
00:02:02,933 --> 00:02:05,000
That's where I have
the advantage.

42
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,300
Andrew...

43
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:12,700
I really want us to try again.

44
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:14,700
Properly this time.

45
00:02:16,067 --> 00:02:19,367
That's why I requested
a transfer here,

46
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,033
and it was approved.

47
00:02:21,167 --> 00:02:23,433
We'll be together more often.

48
00:02:23,567 --> 00:02:28,433
[MELLOW MUSIC]

49
00:02:28,567 --> 00:02:32,000
<i>I'm not good at saying goodbye,
so, I wrote it instead.</i>

50
00:02:32,133 --> 00:02:34,067
<i>But I didn't leave
because I was angry.</i>

51
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:37,400
<i>I love you, you know.
So, how could I be angry?</i>

52
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:41,433
<i> If ever our paths cross again,</i>

53
00:02:41,567 --> 00:02:43,667
<i>I hope everything
is more peaceful.</i>

54
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:46,400
<i> I hope you're truly happy.</i>

55
00:02:46,533 --> 00:02:47,700
<i> I'll miss you.</i>

56
00:02:47,867 --> 00:02:49,067
<i> Peter.</i>

57
00:02:51,033 --> 00:02:54,100
It's heartbreaking, isn't it?
I cried too when I read it.

58
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,367
You read it?

59
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:58,500
Sorry, Joey.

60
00:02:58,633 --> 00:03:00,300
You took too long to come back.

61
00:03:00,433 --> 00:03:02,200
I got impatient. I read it.

62
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:05,667
But you know, Joey,
I realized something about you.

63
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,033
What?

64
00:03:09,267 --> 00:03:10,433
Pretty.

65
00:03:10,567 --> 00:03:12,633
Joey, you're so beautiful.
I applaud you.

66
00:03:12,767 --> 00:03:13,667
Think about it.

67
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,833
You have Peter,
you have Jin Ho bae

68
00:03:16,967 --> 00:03:20,233
who I don't even know
if aliens took him or what.

69
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,200
Then you have Boss Idol too.

70
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:25,767
Girl, you're a fantasy.
You're the fantasy of us gays.

71
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:28,667
What? They're just my friends.

72
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:32,433
But honestly,
I do miss Jin Ho and Peter.

73
00:03:32,567 --> 00:03:36,833
Maybe if they were here,
they could help me and...

74
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:41,000
Who?

75
00:03:41,133 --> 00:03:43,533
What is that? Tamaraw? Tarzan?

76
00:03:43,667 --> 00:03:44,767
Is this a person?

77
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:46,767
What's that, Joey?

78
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,800
No, it's...

79
00:03:48,933 --> 00:03:51,900
it's Tatang,
the old man in our neighborhood.

80
00:03:52,033 --> 00:03:54,000
Because he found another place.

81
00:03:54,167 --> 00:03:56,967
You know, girl, try this.
It's delicious.

82
00:03:57,100 --> 00:04:00,433
At least you'll get salty
about the boys.

83
00:04:02,133 --> 00:04:03,233
Is this good?

84
00:04:03,367 --> 00:04:05,267
It's good, I'm telling you.

85
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:08,100
[CRUNCHES]

86
00:04:11,433 --> 00:04:14,900
Delicious. What's this?
"Crispy mushroom."

87
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:22,600
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

88
00:04:22,733 --> 00:04:24,133
<i> Lumen-X?</i>

89
00:04:24,267 --> 00:04:25,567
<i> That's a party drug.</i>

90
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,200
<i> Popular among the youth.</i>

91
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:29,967
<i>It has a component
of magic mushroom.</i>

92
00:04:31,667 --> 00:04:35,333
[SNAPS]
Hey, why? Isn't it tasty?

93
00:04:35,467 --> 00:04:37,567
No, it's super tasty.

94
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:39,133
Can I take a picture
so I can buy it?

95
00:04:39,267 --> 00:04:41,767
See? I told you.

96
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:46,800
[DAUNTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

97
00:04:46,933 --> 00:04:49,400
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPS]
Thank you very much.

98
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:50,733
[PHONE CHIMES]

99
00:04:50,867 --> 00:04:58,800
[DAUNTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

100
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:03,967
[PHONE RINGING]

101
00:05:04,133 --> 00:05:06,467
- Let me answer this, okay?
- Sure.

102
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:11,167
Hello, Dad?

103
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:12,700
Did you get what I sent?

104
00:05:12,833 --> 00:05:15,100
Yes, child,
the logo and the address.

105
00:05:15,233 --> 00:05:16,133
Yes, Dad.

106
00:05:16,267 --> 00:05:17,233
Good catch, dear.

107
00:05:17,367 --> 00:05:20,000
Looks like I know
where they're making Lumen-X.

108
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:33,333
Everyone out!

109
00:05:35,667 --> 00:05:37,133
You're early.

110
00:05:37,267 --> 00:05:39,433
Is Berdugo here?

111
00:05:39,567 --> 00:05:41,833
No, he still has a meeting.

112
00:05:41,967 --> 00:05:43,500
That's good too.

113
00:05:43,633 --> 00:05:46,400
Isn't it dangerous for him to be
here in the production area?

114
00:05:46,533 --> 00:05:48,200
He's loyal to me,

115
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:50,867
meaning he's loyal
to the organization.

116
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,633
He was one of those chasing us
before.

117
00:05:52,767 --> 00:05:55,767
Lisa, many operations failed

118
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:58,467
because of them
and their companions.

119
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:01,700
If sabotage was my intention,

120
00:06:01,833 --> 00:06:05,067
this operation wouldn't have
lasted long

121
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:06,467
after Lisa brought me in.

122
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,167
Well...

123
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:11,000
this guy actually understands
Tagalog.

124
00:06:11,133 --> 00:06:14,800
So that means you understand...

125
00:06:14,933 --> 00:06:17,067
that I'm not talking to you!

126
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,400
What did he say?

127
00:06:18,533 --> 00:06:19,900
Enough!

128
00:06:20,033 --> 00:06:22,333
Jin Ho, stay out of this.

129
00:06:22,467 --> 00:06:25,233
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:06:25,367 --> 00:06:29,433
Lisa, won't this be a hindrance
to our operation?

131
00:06:29,567 --> 00:06:31,133
Wait a minute.

132
00:06:31,267 --> 00:06:33,733
Did I hit my head somewhere

133
00:06:33,867 --> 00:06:36,400
or did something change
in this organization

134
00:06:36,533 --> 00:06:37,800
without anyone telling me?

135
00:06:37,933 --> 00:06:43,033
Because last time I checked,
I invested in this organization.

136
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:45,633
Berdugo might keep me
beneath him,

137
00:06:45,767 --> 00:06:53,633
but I bring capital, leverage,
and I pay the men here.

138
00:06:53,767 --> 00:06:58,100
Men like you, Matias.

139
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:03,933
I'm very much aware
that Berdugo trusts you,

140
00:07:04,067 --> 00:07:07,367
but that doesn't put you
above me.

141
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:10,167
So don't talk to me like I work
for you.

142
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,667
Know your place!

143
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:17,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

144
00:07:17,633 --> 00:07:21,633
<i>This man with his back turned,
that's Berdugo,</i>

145
00:07:21,767 --> 00:07:24,433
<i> the creator of this damn drug.</i>

146
00:07:25,267 --> 00:07:27,500
<i>He escaped the operation
in the North,</i>

147
00:07:27,633 --> 00:07:31,167
<i>but I'm sure his world
is shrinking.</i>

148
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:35,733
<i>And next time,
there won't be any escape.</i>

149
00:07:35,867 --> 00:07:37,933
<i> It's prison time.</i>

150
00:07:38,067 --> 00:07:40,467
<i>You can count on it,
Tirada viewers,</i>

151
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,267
<i> as always.</i>

152
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:47,333
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

153
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,433
Ma'am Rebecca...

154
00:07:51,667 --> 00:07:53,100
take your medicine.

155
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,533
Thank you.

156
00:07:57,067 --> 00:07:59,100
Clarissa...

157
00:07:59,233 --> 00:08:03,467
The news I used to report
was bad,

158
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:05,767
but now it's worse.

159
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,267
Like this...

160
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:09,900
Like Andrew's report.

161
00:08:10,033 --> 00:08:11,667
Ma'am.

162
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,600
Social media is really toxic
now.

163
00:08:14,733 --> 00:08:18,233
Even I stopped using it.

164
00:08:18,367 --> 00:08:20,633
Better. Good for you.

165
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,700
Good thing...

166
00:08:22,833 --> 00:08:25,300
Good thing my grandchildren
are here.

167
00:08:26,367 --> 00:08:29,067
They're the only ones
I should look at.

168
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,233
They relieve stress.

169
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,933
That's true, Ma'am.

170
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,733
You're lucky.

171
00:08:38,867 --> 00:08:41,900
It's really fun to watch them.

172
00:08:42,033 --> 00:08:43,867
They're happy,

173
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,500
they live a comfortable life.

174
00:08:46,633 --> 00:08:49,033
<i>Then let me just remind you,
Rebecca.</i>

175
00:08:49,167 --> 00:08:52,600
<i>It wasn't this network
that gave you the safety</i>

176
00:08:52,733 --> 00:08:55,233
<i>and comfortable life
you have now.</i>

177
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:57,267
<i> It was me, Rebecca.</i>

178
00:08:59,767 --> 00:09:03,300
Ma'am, did I say something
wrong?

179
00:09:03,433 --> 00:09:04,600
No.

180
00:09:04,733 --> 00:09:07,233
I just remembered something.

181
00:09:07,367 --> 00:09:08,300
Mom...

182
00:09:09,333 --> 00:09:10,433
Are you okay?

183
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:18,333
Lately, you seem a bit distant
and distracted, Mom.

184
00:09:19,467 --> 00:09:20,967
I'm fine.

185
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,633
It's...

186
00:09:22,767 --> 00:09:27,233
It's probably my medicines.
I take so many.

187
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:33,267
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,900
Harris, grandson.

189
00:09:35,033 --> 00:09:36,233
Yes?

190
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:37,867
Where's Kisses?

191
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,600
Kisses is already asleep,
Grandmother.

192
00:09:40,733 --> 00:09:47,067
You remember the brown stuffed
bear I gave her

193
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,433
for her birthday?

194
00:09:48,567 --> 00:09:49,933
The brown one?

195
00:09:50,067 --> 00:09:50,633
The brown...

196
00:09:50,767 --> 00:09:51,533
yes.

197
00:09:51,667 --> 00:09:53,700
- Harold, right?
- Yeah, yeah.

198
00:09:53,833 --> 00:09:54,500
Yes.

199
00:09:54,633 --> 00:09:56,033
Where is it?

200
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:58,533
Mom, I stored it in the
warehouse

201
00:09:58,667 --> 00:10:01,467
so it wouldn't gather dust.

202
00:10:01,633 --> 00:10:03,000
Why, Mom?

203
00:10:03,133 --> 00:10:04,500
Do you need it?

204
00:10:04,633 --> 00:10:06,033
I just remembered.

205
00:10:06,167 --> 00:10:07,667
I just remembered.

206
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:10,833
But can I see it?

207
00:10:10,967 --> 00:10:13,133
- I'll get it for you, Mom.
- We'll get it for you, Mom.

208
00:10:13,267 --> 00:10:14,800
Thank you.

209
00:10:14,933 --> 00:10:17,633
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

210
00:10:17,767 --> 00:10:19,067
I'll just get this.

211
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,300
Thank you.

212
00:10:21,633 --> 00:10:24,633
[DAUNTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

213
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:47,767
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

214
00:10:57,567 --> 00:11:07,533
[DAUNTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

215
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,033
Ma'am...

216
00:11:10,567 --> 00:11:12,933
What are you doing?

217
00:11:13,067 --> 00:11:15,433
Is there anything I can help you
with?

218
00:11:15,567 --> 00:11:18,700
You surprised me, Clarissa.

219
00:11:18,833 --> 00:11:20,867
Nothing, you can't help.

220
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,300
Here.

221
00:11:22,433 --> 00:11:23,567
What is that?

222
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:29,133
It's a spy camera attached
to the eye of the stuffed toy.

223
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,533
And why do you need that?

224
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:36,733
Ma'am Rebecca, I'm not going
to do anything bad to you.

225
00:11:36,867 --> 00:11:39,133
I'm not a bad person, Ma'am.

226
00:11:39,267 --> 00:11:41,133
I know.

227
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:43,200
And this isn't for you.

228
00:11:44,967 --> 00:11:47,000
There's someone I need to catch.

229
00:11:47,133 --> 00:11:49,833
It needs to stop.

230
00:11:49,967 --> 00:11:55,767
It needs to end here
before my family gets hurt.

231
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:58,767
Ma'am, what are you saying?

232
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:12,400
[DOORBELL CHIMES]

233
00:12:12,533 --> 00:12:13,400
Joey.

234
00:12:15,133 --> 00:12:16,800
Joey, what are you doing here?

235
00:12:19,133 --> 00:12:21,067
I'm picking up my mother.

236
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:27,633
[DOORBELL CHIMES]
Wait, wait, Joey.

237
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:31,833
Aren't we going to talk about

238
00:12:31,967 --> 00:12:34,133
what happened to us
in the north?

239
00:12:34,267 --> 00:12:35,767
Which one?

240
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,000
There were many.

241
00:12:37,133 --> 00:12:40,333
The drug deal, Berdugo,
what happened with you and Zoey.

242
00:12:40,467 --> 00:12:42,300
What happened with us.

243
00:12:42,433 --> 00:12:45,500
Can you please not be loud?
What "us"?

244
00:12:45,633 --> 00:12:48,000
Someone might hear you and think
we're still together.

245
00:12:48,167 --> 00:12:49,467
Then Zoey will fight
with me again.

246
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:52,100
Can we not bring Zoey into this?

247
00:12:52,233 --> 00:12:55,100
Wow, protective?

248
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:56,267
Oh, please.

249
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:58,900
You're the one who insisted
she join our mission.

250
00:12:59,033 --> 00:13:01,633
You even excluded me,
didn't you?

251
00:13:04,733 --> 00:13:06,833
Don't say you don't know
about protocol,

252
00:13:06,967 --> 00:13:09,133
-you even made a deal with them.
-No, Joey.

253
00:13:09,267 --> 00:13:11,067
You know, because...

254
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,767
<i> Good evening, Sir Andrew.</i>

255
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,767
Is Mommy Clarissa here?

256
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,200
<i> Are you Joey?</i>

257
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:19,500
She's inside.

258
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:21,100
Wait a moment, I'll open
the door for Sir Andrew,

259
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:22,600
then we'll go in, okay?

260
00:13:22,733 --> 00:13:25,700
No need, Miss,
just escort Joey.

261
00:13:25,833 --> 00:13:27,500
I'll take care of this.

262
00:13:27,633 --> 00:13:30,067
All right. Come on.

263
00:13:32,267 --> 00:13:33,700
<i> This way.</i>

264
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:38,233
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

265
00:13:38,367 --> 00:13:40,133
[KNOCK ON THE DOOR]

266
00:13:45,267 --> 00:13:47,600
[KNOCK ON THE DOOR]

267
00:13:53,067 --> 00:13:58,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

268
00:14:00,833 --> 00:14:02,667
[KNOCK ON THE DOOR]

269
00:14:05,333 --> 00:14:06,700
Come in!

270
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:12,933
[DOOR CLOSE]

271
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:18,033
You wanted to talk to me,
Rebecca?

272
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:22,433
I don't want to lie
to my family anymore.

273
00:14:24,167 --> 00:14:27,333
Tell them who you really are!

274
00:14:30,733 --> 00:14:32,667
That was quite sudden, Rebecca.

275
00:14:34,367 --> 00:14:36,300
And "who I really am?"

276
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:41,033
You mean the man who kept
this family afloat,

277
00:14:41,167 --> 00:14:44,533
paid the bills, fixed the mess?

278
00:14:44,667 --> 00:14:46,533
Who made sure your children

279
00:14:46,667 --> 00:14:50,133
and grandchildren never
lacked anything

280
00:14:50,267 --> 00:14:56,600
while you were cared
for by your physical therapists

281
00:14:56,733 --> 00:14:58,933
and private nurses?

282
00:14:59,067 --> 00:15:02,800
Which, by the way,
I'm still paying for.

283
00:15:02,967 --> 00:15:07,267
You're the reason I ended up
like this!

284
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:11,367
Now, I want you to tell them
everything

285
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:14,833
because I'm sick and tired
of all your lies.

286
00:15:14,967 --> 00:15:17,167
I've carried them long enough.

287
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:20,333
Tell your family who you
really are,

288
00:15:20,467 --> 00:15:23,000
that you are the leader
of a syndicate,

289
00:15:23,133 --> 00:15:24,933
that illegal drugs
are your business,

290
00:15:25,067 --> 00:15:26,733
and that you are Berdugo!

291
00:15:26,867 --> 00:15:30,267
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

292
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:35,067
Here's the address, look.

293
00:15:37,467 --> 00:15:39,067
Yes, this is it.

294
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,500
But this isn't a factory.

295
00:15:40,633 --> 00:15:41,800
This is our house.

296
00:15:41,933 --> 00:15:43,100
We've lived here a long time,

297
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:47,400
and I don't know of any mushroom
chips factory in our area.

298
00:15:47,533 --> 00:15:48,567
All right.

299
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:52,933
[PHONE RINGING]

300
00:15:54,667 --> 00:15:55,267
Sir?

301
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:57,133
<i> I just read your message.</i>

302
00:15:57,267 --> 00:15:59,233
<i>What are you doing there
in Sta. Isabel?</i>

303
00:15:59,367 --> 00:16:03,300
Sir, I feel Berdugo's laboratory
is here.

304
00:16:03,433 --> 00:16:04,867
The address listed is different.

305
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,800
So, we wouldn't track them
I presume.

306
00:16:08,967 --> 00:16:12,267
But I think, Sir, we're close.

307
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:14,000
Come, come in.

308
00:16:14,133 --> 00:16:16,200
Sit down first, Joey.

309
00:16:16,333 --> 00:16:18,800
I'll just tell your mother
you're here.

310
00:16:18,933 --> 00:16:20,533
I think she's still doing
something in the kitchen.

311
00:16:20,667 --> 00:16:21,433
Thank you.

312
00:16:21,567 --> 00:16:23,000
All right.
I'll leave you for now.

313
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:36,467
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

314
00:16:44,067 --> 00:16:45,200
Joey.

315
00:16:46,767 --> 00:16:48,367
I just want to be clear.

316
00:16:49,433 --> 00:16:52,733
I did not intend to kick you out
of the operations.

317
00:16:52,867 --> 00:16:54,667
It was protocol.

318
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:56,700
Protocol again.

319
00:16:56,833 --> 00:17:00,833
Do you think I'll really believe
you didn't know I'd be excluded?

320
00:17:00,967 --> 00:17:02,400
You're a journalist.

321
00:17:02,533 --> 00:17:04,333
You're smart.

322
00:17:04,467 --> 00:17:07,133
So, it's impossible
you didn't know I'd be barred

323
00:17:07,267 --> 00:17:08,367
from that operation
from the start.

324
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:09,300
I know.

325
00:17:09,433 --> 00:17:11,567
See? You admitted it.

326
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:14,000
Yes, yes, but wait.

327
00:17:15,067 --> 00:17:17,867
I knew, but I realized it late.

328
00:17:19,067 --> 00:17:21,400
You think they'll believe you?

329
00:17:21,533 --> 00:17:28,333
A woman in constant pain,
on heavy meds, emotional?

330
00:17:28,467 --> 00:17:29,933
What do you think they'll hear?

331
00:17:30,067 --> 00:17:33,433
Maybe they won't believe me

332
00:17:33,567 --> 00:17:36,233
because you poisoned
their minds,

333
00:17:36,367 --> 00:17:38,867
because you touched
their hearts.

334
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,833
But I know there are still those
who will believe me.

335
00:17:42,967 --> 00:17:46,100
Your lies should end tonight.

336
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:48,300
I'm going to tell my children.

337
00:17:50,167 --> 00:17:55,733
- [GRUNTING]
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:57,000
Joey...

339
00:17:59,533 --> 00:18:00,967
Sir Andrew.

340
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:02,067
Miss Clarissa.

341
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:05,567
Are you here to visit
Ma'am Rebecca?

342
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:09,067
Yes, Miss Clarissa.

343
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,567
By the way,

344
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:15,167
my sister mentioned that my mom
feels comfortable with you,

345
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:21,500
and that rarely happens
with her caregivers.

346
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:24,033
Well, your mom is kind.

347
00:18:24,167 --> 00:18:25,600
Are we going home?

348
00:18:25,733 --> 00:18:28,200
Dear, that's what I was going
to tell you.

349
00:18:28,333 --> 00:18:32,333
I'm not finished preparing
Ma'am Rebecca's herbal medicine.

350
00:18:32,467 --> 00:18:34,967
Ma'am Yvette will just let
the driver bring me home.

351
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:37,200
But I was thinking,
what about you?

352
00:18:38,633 --> 00:18:42,067
I'll take Joey home,
Miss Clarissa.

353
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:44,867
Oh no, don't.
You'll be inconvenienced.

354
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,200
Don't.

355
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:51,033
No, it's okay because mommy
will sleep later anyway, right?

356
00:18:51,167 --> 00:18:55,033
And just think of it
as my way of repaying

357
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:57,167
all the good you've done
for my mom.

358
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,400
I don't want to.

359
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:04,333
Don't be like that to your mom.
Don't add to her problems, Joey.

360
00:19:04,467 --> 00:19:05,800
Come on.

361
00:19:06,767 --> 00:19:10,933
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

362
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:12,600
Go on, Joey.

363
00:19:12,733 --> 00:19:15,267
Sir Andrew is offering anyway.

364
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:17,233
It would be rude to refuse.

365
00:19:18,767 --> 00:19:20,067
Go on.

366
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,133
Shall we go?

367
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:28,800
Text me, Mom, okay?
I'll wait for you to get home.

368
00:19:28,967 --> 00:19:31,467
All right.
Text me too when you get home?

369
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,100
- All right.
- Love you.

370
00:19:33,233 --> 00:19:34,100
Love you.

371
00:19:34,233 --> 00:19:38,000
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

372
00:19:40,567 --> 00:19:42,167
I'm telling my children now!

373
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:47,967
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- [GRUNTING]

374
00:19:48,767 --> 00:19:52,500
- [THUDS]
- [GROANS]

375
00:19:52,633 --> 00:19:56,867
[INDISTINCT CHATTER ON TV]

376
00:19:59,233 --> 00:20:01,700
I feel no mercy for you anymore.

377
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:06,667
- [THUDDING]
- [GROANING]

378
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:19,000
You've been too emotional
lately.

379
00:20:20,833 --> 00:20:27,767
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER ON TV]
- [GROANING]

380
00:20:29,133 --> 00:20:30,733
This should help you relax.

381
00:20:32,333 --> 00:20:34,000
By this time tomorrow,

382
00:20:35,267 --> 00:20:37,767
you won't even remember this
conversation.

383
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:45,733
- [STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [GRAPS]

384
00:20:50,667 --> 00:20:59,167
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER ON TV]
- [STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

385
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,700
Bro.

386
00:21:04,767 --> 00:21:07,300
Do you know if there's a food
processing factory

387
00:21:07,433 --> 00:21:08,333
here in Sta. Isabel?

388
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:09,667
None, Bro.

389
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:10,433
None?

390
00:21:10,567 --> 00:21:12,500
They're making mushroom chips.

391
00:21:14,467 --> 00:21:15,667
None, Sir.

392
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:18,167
- All right, thanks.
- All right, Sir.

393
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:30,567
- [REVVING]
- [DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

394
00:21:34,567 --> 00:21:41,000
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

395
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:42,333
<i> Sir.</i>

396
00:21:43,767 --> 00:21:44,933
Can you check this?

397
00:21:45,067 --> 00:21:46,300
All right.

398
00:21:47,867 --> 00:21:51,133
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:55,833
Is that the Korean, your crush?

400
00:21:55,967 --> 00:22:00,300
<i>He's not my crush, okay.
Jin Ho is just really funny.</i>

401
00:22:00,433 --> 00:22:07,933
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

402
00:22:08,067 --> 00:22:10,333
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPS]

403
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:16,867
[INDISTINCT CHATTER ON TV]

404
00:22:17,633 --> 00:22:19,500
Ma'am Rebecca...

405
00:22:19,633 --> 00:22:21,367
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

406
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:22,933
Ma'am Rebecca?

407
00:22:24,267 --> 00:22:26,033
Ma'am Rebecca...

408
00:22:26,167 --> 00:22:28,367
What did you do, Ma'am Rebecca?

409
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:30,333
Ma'am Rebecca!

410
00:22:30,467 --> 00:22:33,533
Ma'am Yvette!

411
00:22:33,667 --> 00:22:40,067
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

412
00:22:41,833 --> 00:22:43,933
Your Korean friend,
do you still talk to him?

413
00:22:44,067 --> 00:22:46,600
Maybe he already caught
the syndicate member

414
00:22:46,733 --> 00:22:47,800
he was looking for.

415
00:22:47,933 --> 00:22:49,100
Please save my mommy.

416
00:22:49,267 --> 00:22:51,633
What happened?
Why did you leave her alone?

417
00:22:51,767 --> 00:22:54,767
I can't handle it if something
happens to Ma'am Rebecca.

418
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:56,367
There's no Lee Jin Ho
in the database.

419
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:58,500
That only means one thing.
He's not Korean police.

420
00:22:58,633 --> 00:23:01,033
- She's in critical condition.
- It looks intentional.

421
00:23:01,167 --> 00:23:03,000
- Mommy couldn't have done that.
- Andrew...

422
00:23:03,133 --> 00:23:04,100
Let's start CPR.

423
00:23:04,233 --> 00:23:05,300
Mom, fight, please.

424
00:23:05,433 --> 00:23:09,933
You cannot live, Rebecca.
They cannot know the truth.
